1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:03,063
London, the early thirteen hundreds.

2
00:00:03,013 --> 00:00:04,526
You are a baker's boy,

3
00:00:04,476 --> 00:00:06,859
and the loaf in your hands is a little too

4
00:00:06,809 --> 00:00:07,823
light.

5
00:00:07,889 --> 00:00:09,274
Not by much.

6
00:00:09,224 --> 00:00:11,051
Nobody would notice.

7
00:00:11,094 --> 00:00:12,119
Somebody will.

8
00:00:12,069 --> 00:00:14,046
This city weighs its bread.

9
00:00:13,996 --> 00:00:16,891
The price of grain sets how heavy a penny loaf

10
00:00:16,841 --> 00:00:20,339
must be, and men come to the shop to check.

11
00:00:20,382 --> 00:00:23,416
Here is what happens to a baker whose bread comes

12
00:00:23,366 --> 00:00:24,205
up short.

13
00:00:24,155 --> 00:00:26,771
The first time, he is tied to a hurdle and

14
00:00:26,721 --> 00:00:28,698
dragged through the dirtiest streets,

15
00:00:28,648 --> 00:00:30,138
where the most people are.

16
00:00:30,088 --> 00:00:32,866
The light loaf hangs from his neck.

17
00:00:32,874 --> 00:00:35,402
The second time, the pillory.

18
00:00:35,352 --> 00:00:39,001
One hour, in front of everyone who buys from him.

19
00:00:39,044 --> 00:00:41,764
The third time, they pull down his oven.

20
00:00:41,714 --> 00:00:44,469
He never bakes in this city again.

21
00:00:44,519 --> 00:00:47,255
So you put the loaf back on the scale.

22
00:00:47,205 --> 00:00:49,031
You add dough.

23
00:00:49,051 --> 00:00:52,320
That is what an ordinary life is.

24
00:00:52,270 --> 00:00:53,621
Not small.

25
00:00:53,571 --> 00:00:56,999
Just weighed, every single day.
